Package: com.duoface.carplay.nativescenehost
Name: DuoFace Native Dashboard Scene Host (Development)
Version: 0.1.175~touchfix1
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Section: Development
Maintainer: DuoFace Independent
Depends: firmware (>= 16.0), mobilesubstrate
Description: QA175 touch reliability: pane-only root touch fall-through (QA173's version broke divider drags and leaked sheet taps), trailing-edge scene geometry commits with retry (was one-shot/per-pass in QA173), single-source divider visibility so the logo grip always returns, surface observers registered once after guards, GOFA shadow decoder moved to a serial queue (was racing on GOFA's thread); diagnostic build labels now name the current build (QA174 fix). Keeps the QA172 GOFA payload decoder in shadow mode (bubble speed stays GPS) and cuts diagnostic logging (de-duplicated, state-change-only, 256 KiB rotation), commits hosted-scene geometry in the same layout pass instead of deferring 0.30s, and adds a flag-gated root-window touch fall-through (default on) for hosted apps such as YouTube. Road speed limits/cameras/live route UNVERIFIED; QA162 GOFA-only Speed8 trial (no guessed road limit), plus QA161 scoped first SOLO remote geometry reference 120ms instead of 300ms, preserving media and split safety gates; retains QA160 read-only CarPlay Home trace. Native Home app-grid destination NOT fixed or physically tested. First-party experimental iOS16 rootless CarPlay Native12 integrated candidate with live app cards/recent, logo loading scene, touch activity borders, safer scene resize and foreground-only chrome. Real installed-app picker, source-owned external SBAppViewController host, two visible empty split panes with pass-through input, two clickable controls per pane, scene-ready/failure signals, split/swap/focus/drag and strict disconnect/heartbeat teardown. The CarPlay receiver draws no demo panes or fake action buttons; iPhone shows only actual installed-app inventory and active-session status. No external vendor binary or licensing; actual dual-app rendering and touch on iPhone X/CarPlay not yet device-verified. Opt-in 10-second physical disconnect per-process RunningBoard close with app PID provenance, reconnect cancel and phone foreground guard. Source-verified stage only; CarPlay native map tile/navigation and full iPhone auto-launch or screen-off are not device-verified. Unreleased QA candidate.
